  "notes": "Sony BRAVIA XBR-65X900E (2017, BRAVIA_ATV2, MediaTek), US/Canada firmware\nAndroid TV 9, build PTT1.190515.001.S54\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/sony-xbr-x900e/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/sony-xbr-x900e/debloat.txt\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.tvlauncher (restore.sh's default).\nLive TV / input app: com.sony.dtv.tvx. Keep it: it also plays every HDMI input.\nKeep: com.sony.dtv.tvinput.*, braviasync* (HDMI-CEC), remotepairing, rcpowerkey, uinputservice,\nimeproxy, sonysystemservice, settingsprovider, all com.mediatek.* and mtktvapi.agent, timers (sleep timer).\nLeft alone on purpose: the rest of com.sony.dtv.b2b.* (hotel/pro mode plumbing), webapi.core and\nremoteaccess (Sony IP control, possibly used by Alexa control).\nAlready disabled at the factory/by owner: com.sony.rvu, actionmenu.plugin.harmony, Vudu, Crackle,\ncom.google.android.inputmethod.latin. Not in this list so restore.sh leaves them off.\n\nNotes from this firmware:\n- The stock launcher's HOME filter has priority 2, so `cmd package set-home-activity` reports Success\nbut Home keeps opening it until com.google.android.tvlauncher is disabled (build-and-install.sh\ndoes this last). Launch com.gathin.tvhome/.MainActivity with `am start -n` to check it first.\n- Inputs works: com.sony.dtv.tvx handles the passthrough channel URIs, HDMI 1-4 and Video 1/2 listed.\nHide com.sony.dtv.tvx and com.sony.dtv.tvxlauncher.programguide in config.xml; set\nlive_tv_package to com.sony.dtv.tvx if you use an antenna.\n- 2 GB RAM. Survives a reboot straight into the new launcher.\nACR viewing tracker",
